# The C++ clang-tidy checks, for the compiled core and the Hydra bridge (tools/feasibility/hydra_bridge/), run by
# pre-commit through tools/clang_tidy.py. At the root, so clang-tidy and editors find it from either project.
# Every warning fails.
# Left out:
# - trailing return types (a style choice) and include-cleaner, which can't follow pxr's umbrella headers;
# - from the C++ Core Guidelines checks: unchecked container access and constant array indices, which flag every
#   subscript, though the code validates indices before it uses them; reference and const data
#   members, which short-lived helper classes hold on purpose; and magic numbers;
# - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters, which flags any two adjacent parameters of one type; the bridge's
#   Python entry points take them as keyword arguments;
# - the analyzer's leak check (cplusplus.NewDeleteLeaks), which reports inside USD's TfNotice::Register, whose
#   registry owns what it allocates; cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory covers the code's own allocations.
# A NOLINT names its check and says why the code needs the exception.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-cplusplus.NewDeleteLeaks,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-const-or-ref-data-members,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index,
  misc-*,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  modernize-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  performance-*
WarningsAsErrors: "*"
CheckOptions:
  # A struct whose members are all public is a plain record, even with a method or two.
  misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes.IgnoreClassesWithAllMemberVariablesBeingPublic: true
